            <ArticleTitle>Does regular exercise reduce the pain and stiffness of osteoarthritis?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>476-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Exercise helps reduce the pain, but it's unclear whether it helps with stiffness. Exercise moderately reduces pain in elderly patients with osteoarthritis and has a small effect on reducing self-reported disability. No studies have evaluated the effect of exercise on stiffness.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
